Z||000000||wkayl||07-21-2001||12:07 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/leftrear_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hitch.jpg"> <BR>Above the arrow pionts to the bolt holding the hitch to the car.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bolt.jpg"> <BR>There is only one bolt on each side.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/standing.jpg"> <BR>It is strong enough for me to stand on the hitch (no fat jokes please)<BR>[img]<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000001||wkayl||07-21-2001||12:08 AM||||   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/topside_1.jpg"> <BR>I made a place to hold a gas can so I can make it 300 miles between fillups (helps when driving through northern Nebraska and southern South Dakota.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/plug_1.jpg">   I spliced into the liscense plate light wires for tail lights.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rear_9.jpg">   <BR>I don't use turn or brake lights because you can see them from the rear.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 07-21-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 07-21-2001).]||||reg||1
